"text": "                     District faces a significant risk of prolonged service outages, during which critical repairs\n                     could not be completed. The SCADA system needs to be updated to more current\n                     technology with a new service provider that can serve the District in the future.\n         Project The Moapa Valley Water District proposes to improve the existing SCADA system. The\n        Narrative existing system is dated, inefficient, and will soon be unserviceable. The project will\n                  replace and install over 140 SCADA system components, including flow meters, pumps,\n                  valves, sensors, and switches across 38 different sites.",
